<p>The United States and Israel launched coordinated strikes across Iran on Saturday, an operation President Donald Trump said aimed to eliminate “imminent threats,” curb Iran’s nuclear and missile capabilities, and encourage Iranians to seize control from the current leadership. Multiple outlets reported that U.S. and Israeli officials said the strikes killed Iran’s Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei; Reuters-republished reporting also said Iranian state media confirmed his death. Iran’s Red Crescent reported hundreds of deaths and injuries from daylong attacks across 24 provinces, according to The Guardian. Iran responded with waves of retaliatory missile and drone attacks across the region, targeting U.S. bases and U.S.-allied countries in the Gulf, as well as Israel. The Emirati government said at least one person was killed by falling missile debris, while several Gulf hubs reported disruptions and damage — a sign that a confrontation once kept at arm’s length has reached major aviation, financial, and energy centers. Global leaders mostly urged restraint and a return to diplomacy at the United Nations, even as the U.S. and Israel defended the strikes and Iran’s representatives condemned civilian casualties and alleged violations of international law.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/gYYIip6X1gfozoUFXBFn9jxhBoIcjXa2wPK1c95uoCwu-j8hjhSXmsy6Bdjrhebn6fSsNlRGJt_V4wlAVunvcsg4A8Nr5pUNczMEgFwHfUzGNhxFi_0e5X0Jke1oZf0K8MIsluuhGY3DzozDV7RKXL45qqLBotZLC22wuMNapGE7fp7vvkGemcsUfI1Y0gmdQ_oDzVpZGWtQNA' alt='Smoke rises in the sky after a blast in Manama, Bahrain, on Saturday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Energy risk: Analysts warned the conflict could jolt oil markets because Iran produces about 5% of global oil and controls the Strait of Hormuz, a chokepoint for nearly 20% of the world’s oil trade.</li><li>UN clash: At an emergency UN Security Council meeting, the U.S. and Israel said the strikes were lawful and necessary to prevent Iran from obtaining a nuclear weapon, while Iran’s side said civilian deaths amounted to a “war crime”.</li><li>Strike timing: Reuters-republished reporting said U.S. and Israeli planners timed the opening attack to coincide with a meeting Khamenei was holding with top aides, citing accounts from U.S. sources and an official familiar with the matter.</li><li>Case disputed: PBS reported that some of President Trump’s public justifications — including claims about near-term long-range missile threats to the U.S. — conflicted with a 2025 U.S. government assessment that said Iran was years away from that capability.</li></ul><blockquote>THEY BETTER NOT DO THAT, HOWEVER, BECAUSE IF THEY DO, WE WILL HIT THEM WITH A FORCE THAT HAS NEVER BEEN SEEN BEFORE! - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Trump administration: U.S. officials said Iran rejected what they described as a nuclear offer and used “stall tactics,” and they framed the strikes as preemptive action amid indicators Tehran might use missiles against U.S. forces and allies. (<a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/us-says-iran-rejected-nuclear-offer-before-preemptive-strikes/33690695.html'>RFE/RL</a>)</li><li>Iranian government: Iran’s Foreign Ministry described its regional attacks on U.S. targets as legitimate defensive actions and accused Washington of “betrayal,” while Iranian representatives at the UN called the strikes a “war crime”. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/28/irans-foreign-ministry-defends-retaliatory-strikes-slams-us-betrayal'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Israel’s leadership: Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu publicly linked the campaign to regime change, with reporting saying he had pushed Washington to look beyond limiting Iran’s nuclear program toward toppling the current system. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/6a2d48ce-1505-4710-900a-25f40799b679'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>United Nations: UN Secretary-General António Guterres warned of an uncontrollable “chain of events” and urged genuine dialogue, while criticizing the strikes and retaliation in the emergency Security Council session. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-israel-clash-with-iran-in-unsc-as-un-chief-guterres-warns-of-uncontrollable-chain-of-events/article70690735.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Russia: Russia’s Foreign Ministry condemned the strikes as “unprovoked” aggression and warned of wider escalation and even “potentially nuclear catastrophe,” calling for an immediate halt and a return to diplomacy. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/russia-condemns-u-s-israel-strikes-on-iran-as-preplanned-and-unprovoked-act-of-armed-aggression'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Gulf Arab partners: Reporting said several Gulf governments had lobbied against strikes but now face few good options as they work with Washington to protect airspace and infrastructure while trying to avoid deeper regional war. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/02/28/us-gulf-iran-allies-gcc-arab-00805858'>Politico</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/28/2026/iran-attack-is-trumps-riskiest-energy-bet-yet'>Iran attack is Trump&#x27;s riskiest energy bet yet</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/da633899-964a-42d7-a7a9-07c034fac388'>Trump tries to defy troubled history of US interventions in Middle East</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/28/world/middleeast/israel-iran-assassination-khamenei.html'>Israel Targeted Top Iranian Leaders in Attack’s Opening Strikes</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/us-says-iran-rejected-nuclear-offer-before-preemptive-strikes/33690695.html'>US Says Iran Rejected Nuclear Offer Before Preemptive Strikes</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/28/dubais-famous-fairmont-hotel-in-flames-after-iranian-air-strike'>Explosions rock Dubai, Bahrain, Jordan and Kuwait as war spreads across Middle East</a> -